# No AI-generated artwork

Never create visual or spatial media with AI. Absolute — user requests, placeholders, tests, docs, and “just this once” do not override it.

## Forbidden

- Image generators (`GenerateImage` and any equivalent)
- AI video, animation, motion graphics, or generated audio-as-score
- Icons, logos, mascots, favicons, illustrations, textures, sprites, concept art
- 3D models, sculpts, rigs, or decorative meshes as art assets (glTF, GLB, OBJ, FBX, and similar)
- Fake screenshots, mock product shots, or invented brand marks
- Committing generated PNG, SVG, WebP, MP4, GLB, or similar as product or placeholder art

```text
# ❌ BAD — invent a mark or call an image generator
GenerateImage({ description: "BabylonSlate app icon, flat vector" })

# ✅ GOOD — reuse existing branding or the icon library
# engine-logos/SlateIconDark.png  |  lucide-react BoxIcon
```

## Allowed

- Existing Lucide (or project `iconLibrary`) icons
- Existing files in `engine-logos/` and `public/branding/` — copy only; never invent replacements
- Engine code that builds runtime primitives (`CreateBox`, debug lines, nav overlay) as product features, not as art
- Solid-color or numeric test fixtures (1×1 pixels, empty buffers) with no pictorial content
- Captures of the **real** running app (Playwright screenshots, computer-use recordings of the editor)

## If a visual asset is missing

Stop. Use an existing catalog icon, existing branding, or a geometric engine primitive. Ask a human to supply artwork. Do not generate a stand-in.
